<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Lufthansa starts repairs at Almaty airport.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa starts repairs at Almaty airport.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Lufthansa AG has begun repairs on the international airport in the Kazakh capital Almaty, an official of the German company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He told Reuters repair work on the airport's runways, to be carried out by German subcontractors Peussehl, would cost DM 1 million.</p>
<p>The Lufthansa official said the repair works meant the Central Asian nation's airport would be operational only at night up until October 31.</p>
<p>Last week, a Kazakhstan Aviation Agency spokesman said that all flights, including international ones, would depart and arrive at Almaty airport at night, but said passengers would be able to buy tickets during the day as usual.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
